+<intent-contract>
+
+## Intent
+
+**Problem:** The walk ends on its last question with Create wallet, so nobody sees all their answers together before creating. Changing Network on step 1 also only resets the Node and an untouched Signing Check, so answers made for the old Network (No Open Check, 30 seconds, Passkey-Derived on an unbound address) stay selected and are met later as blocked options.
+
+**Approach:** Add a Review step at the end of the walk: every applicable answer with a Change button, and Create wallet. A pure reconcile function runs on every Network change: it reads the new Network's legality from `describeOptions`, keeps legal answers, resets illegal ones to the pre-selection, and the flow shows a polite text line naming what was reset.
+
+## Boundaries & Constraints
+
+**Always:**
+- Review is the last step of the walk, after Signing Check, for Generate and Import. Counter: Generate "Step 8 of 8" on the review, Import "Step 6 of 6". The last walk question now shows Next; Create wallet is on step 2 and on the Review only. Both call the same `handleCreate`.
+- Review lists every applicable answer once: Label, Network, Node, Seed Method, Passkey choice (only when Passkey-Derived), Signature type, Open Check, Auto-lock, Signing Check. Import omits Seed Method, Passkey choice and Signature type. Each row has a **Change** button (accessible name "Change <term>", 44px target on coarse pointers) that goes to the step that asks it, with the answer kept.
+- One source for rows. Each `WALK_QUESTIONS` entry gains a `summary` (its rows, each tagged with the step id that asks it) and one formatter per answer is shared by the rows, the step-2 list and the reset line. Step 2's list and the Review read the same rows. A test fails if a registry entry yields no row.
+- After Change, Next goes to the Review, not the next question (assumption in SPEC.md). Back stays one step back. The return flag clears on arriving at the Review. Done in the Flow's `onIndex` wrapper (a forward move while the flag is set goes to the Review); `QuizShell` is not changed.
+- The reconcile reads legality from `describeOptions(next Network)` (`.seedMethod[x].available`, `.openCheck[x].available`, `.autoLock[minutes].available`, `.signing[x].available`). It never re-derives a rule. One `preselection(network, capability)` (Seed Method stored, Open Check passkey if capability is yes else pin, auto-lock 5, Signing Check per `defaultSigning`) is shared by the initial state and the reset.
+- Order: Seed Method first; if Passkey-Derived is kept, Signing Check stays passkey and touched; if it was reset to stored, Signing Check returns to the new pre-selection and is untouched. Then Open Check, auto-lock, and an unavailable Signing Check. A custom Node always resets to built-in (existing behaviour: a Node was proven for one Network only) and is named only when it was custom.
+- An untouched Signing Check keeps following the Network's pre-selection silently, as today. It is not an answer the person made, so it is not named. A Signing Check reset because Seed Method fell back is named.
+- The line is visible text under Network on step 1, in an always-mounted `role="status"` / `aria-live="polite"` region, naming each reset question and its new value (for example "Changed to Mainnet. Reset to the recommended answer: Open Check is now App PIN; Auto-lock is now 5 minutes."). No reset means no line. Each Network change replaces the line; it clears when the step changes. Words or icon, never colour alone; no new colour token.
+- Answers that were reset are not restored if the person switches back.
+- Create wallet still guards `options.combination.ok`, label and custom-Node checks, so policy refuses any illegal combination before any write, as today. Focus goes to the Review heading (the shell already does this). PIN fields show on step 2 and on the Review only (hidden, not unmounted, elsewhere). Import's Seed field stays mounted once. No secret enters state; the Review shows no Seed and no PIN.
+
+**Never:** Change `describeOptions`, `policy.ts`, any pre-selection value, or any legality rule. Hard-code which answers a Network makes illegal. Add or change a question. Change `QuizShell`, Configure, PIN entry, the Seed backup or the written-Seed step. Remove the existing Passkey/Seed/PIN mounting patterns. Animate a step change. Re-add a Recommended panel or Customise toggle (story 5 deletes leftovers).
+
+## I/O & Edge-Case Matrix
+
+| Scenario | Input / State | Expected Output / Behavior | Error Handling |
+|----------|--------------|---------------------------|----------------|
+| Review (Generate) | finish the walk, Next on Signing Check | "Review", "Step 8 of 8", a row and a Change for each applicable answer, Create wallet in the footer, PIN fields if an App PIN is chosen | Blocked verdict shows the existing warning Alert, Create `aria-disabled` |
+| Review (Import) | Import walk | "Step 6 of 6"; no Seed Method, Passkey or Signature type row | n/a |
+| Change then Next | Review, Change on Node, edit, Next | Node step keeps the answer; Next lands on the Review with the edit shown | n/a |
+| Change on Network | Review, Change on Network row | Step 1; Next lands on the Review (Label rules still block Next) | Label error blocks Next as today |
+| Testnet to Mainnet, illegal answers | No Open Check, 30 seconds, custom Node | Open Check to pre-selection, auto-lock to 5, Node to built-in; line names all three | n/a |
+| Testnet to Mainnet, legal answers | App PIN, 15 minutes, Passkey-Derived on a bound host | Kept; no line | n/a |
+| Derived on an unbound or unknown host | Passkey-Derived chosen, Network to Mainnet | Seed Method to Stored, Signing Check to the new pre-selection; both named; Passkey-Derived stays visible, `aria-disabled`, with its reason | n/a |
+| Nothing differs | Network changed with only pre-selections set | No line, no reset | n/a |
+| Back and forth | Reset on Mainnet, back to Testnet | Reset answers stay at pre-selection; a new line only if something resets again | n/a |
+| Create from Review | Same answers as step 2 | Same `createStoredWallet` / `createDerivedWallet` / `importStoredWallet` call as step 2 | Refusals show as today |
+
