+## Design Notes
+
+- Resolved without asking: "legal" means available under `describeOptions` for the new Network. Network alone makes only No Open Check, 30 seconds and Passkey-Derived illegal; passkey-capability illegality does not change with Network and is not touched here.
+- Resolved without asking: a custom Node is reset on every Network change (already so, per the code); it is named only if it was custom. An untouched Signing Check following the Network's pre-selection is not a reset, since the person never chose it.
+- Resolved without asking (SPEC assumption): after Change, Next goes to the Review. Back remains one step back, so no new Back rule is needed; the flag clears on reaching the Review.
+- Resolved without asking: the reset line sits on step 1, the only place Network changes (the Review's Change on Network goes there), and clears when the step changes; the Review shows the reconciled values.
+- The Review row list adds "Passkey" (new or existing) when Passkey-Derived is chosen, because FR-91 says every applicable answer. Step 2 shows it too through the shared rows.
+- Golden example of the reset result:
+  `reconcileForNetwork({ seedMethod: 'stored', openCheck: 'none', autoLockMinutes: 0.5, signing: 'standard', signingTouched: false, nodeMode: 'custom' }, 'mainnet', ctx)` returns Open Check pin or passkey by capability, auto-lock 5, signing `defaultSigning('mainnet')`, Node built-in, and reset `[Open Check, Auto-lock, Node]` (Signing Check not named).
